<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bremer Vulkan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893–1997</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bremer Vulkan was a shipbuilding company founded in 1893 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vegesack">Vegesack</a>, then a town near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a>. It built merchant ships and, in both world wars, warships and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/u-boat">U-boats</a>, and after 1945 grew into a large shipbuilding group. Its collapse in 1996–1997 was one of the largest industrial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereign-default">bankruptcies</a> in post-war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and left Bremen with heavy debts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bremer-vulkan.jpg" alt="Bremer Vulkan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logobremervulkan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
